+/**
+ * @brief Put a larger picture where an image was just loaded into VRAM
+ *
+ * For sharper pictures than the game's: after LoadImage put the native image
+ * at (x, y, w, h) of VRAM, this picture (any size, scaled smoothly) replaces
+ * that rectangle of the renderer's upscaled VRAM, so what is drawn there
+ * next (and the display) shows it at the internal resolution. Native VRAM
+ * keeps the game's image. Does nothing (and returns 0) at internal resolution 1.
